<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pliva</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pliva River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pliva is a river in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a> that flows through the Pliva lakes and joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vrbas">Vrbas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jajce">Jajce</a> in a waterfall over 20 metres high in the centre of the town. Its valley formed part of the defences of Jajce, the royal Bosnian fortress that became the seat of a Hungarian banate after 1463, guarding the route into central Bosnia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pliva.jpg" alt="Pliva" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suradnik13 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pliva_Upravna_zgrada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
